dex task at $0.01, followed by Granite 4.2 8B ($0.02) and Ling 3.0 Flash ($0.03)."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Which is the best open weights model on the leaderboard?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Kimi K3 (max) is the highest-ranked open weights model with an Intelligence Index score of 50. There are 18 open weights models out of 55 total on the leaderboard."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What are the top open weights models on the leaderboard?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The top open weights models by Intelligence Index are: 1. Kimi K3 (max) (50), 2. GLM-5.3 (max) (49), 3. Qwen3.8 2.4T A95B (47)."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Which is the best reasoning model on the leaderboard?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Claude Fable 5.1 (Adaptive Reasoning, Max Effort, Default Fallback) leads among 53 reasoning models with an Intelligence Index score of 57. Reasoning models use extended thinking to solve complex problems before responding."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do I filter models on the leaderboard?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The leaderboard includes filters to narrow results by model type (reasoning vs non-reasoning), openness (open weights vs proprietary), and other criteria. You can also adjust prompt options to see how performance varies with different input lengths."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Where can I see more detailed metrics for a model?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Click on any model name in the leaderboard to visit its dedicated comparison page with detailed charts covering intelligence, pricing, speed, latency, and more. You can also compare API providers for each model."}}]}</script></div></div></div><!--$--><!--/$--><section aria-label="Notifications alt+T" tabindex="-1" aria-live="polite" aria-relevant="additions text" aria-atomic="false"></section><div class="pointer-events-none fixed bottom-6 right-6 z-50 flex flex-col items-end gap-4"><button class="inline-flex i